  "title": "2026-07-25-eval-160035 · agent-session-orchestration",
  "description": "# Long-lived agent session orchestration\n\nA left-to-right, top-to-bottom lifecycle map for sessions running through a shared control plane. The top row covers intake, placement, iterative model/tool execution, and client streaming with durable event replay. The middle row shows content-addressed checkpoints and forks, crash recovery with idempotent replay, and interruption into a safe resumable checkpoint. The bottom row shows child-session propagation and reaping, tree/workspace quota decisions with audit metering, and version-aware host draining. Dashed cross-section links show the control relationships between execution, durability, quotas, recovery, cancellation, child sessions, and deployment shutdown.",
